IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-definitions`
IMPORT `P8-gate`

-- P8-art74: Article 74, market surveillance and control of AI systems in the Union market (Chapter IX Section 3). LAYER 1.
-- Group General (from 2 August 2026). The Omnibus did not change Article 74. Most paragraphs allocate powers and designations to authorities
-- and Member States: they are encoded for what they decide, and (in the seat layer) for what they mean to a provider, deployer, importer,
-- distributor, authorised representative or product manufacturer. Paragraphs 12 and 13 put duties on providers.
-- The consolidated text is a rendering with no legal effect.

DECLARE `Art 74 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 74(2) report annually to the Commission and the relevant national competition authorities the information of potential interest for competition rules`
    `Art 74(2) report annually to the Commission about the use of prohibited practices and the measures taken`
    `Art 74(8) designate as market surveillance authorities the data protection supervisory authorities or another authority`
    `Art 74(10) facilitate coordination between market surveillance authorities and other relevant national authorities or bodies`
    `Art 74(11) provide coordination support for joint investigations`
    `Art 74(12) grant the market surveillance authorities full access to the documentation and the training, validation and testing data sets`
    `Art 74(13) grant the market surveillance authority access to the source code of the high-risk AI system`
    `Art 74(14) treat the information or documentation obtained in accordance with the confidentiality obligations set out in Article 78`

§ `Article 74(1): Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 applies`

-- src:1147 | 1. Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 shall apply to AI systems covered by this Regulation. For the purposes of the effective enforcement of this Regulation:
@ref Art 74(1) introductory words (src:1147)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system is covered by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(1) Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 applies to the AI system` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the AI system is covered by this Regulation`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 applies to "AI systems covered by this Regulation"

-- (a): "any reference to an economic operator under Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 shall be understood as including all operators identified in Article 2(1)".
-- The role is the core's `Role`; the six operators of Art 3(8) are the operators; a notified body and an affected person are not operators.
-- src:1148 | (a) any reference to an economic operator under Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 shall be understood as including all operators identified in Article 2(1) of this Regulation;
@ref Art 74(1)(a) (src:1148)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the role of the party` IS A Role
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(1)(a) the party is understood as an economic operator under Regulation (EU) 2019/1020` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `Art 3(8) the role is an operator` `the role of the party`
         THEN JUST TRUE  -- "shall be understood as including all operators identified in Article 2(1)"
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the text says what a reference is "understood as including"; it does not say that no one else is an economic operator

-- src:1149 | (b) any reference to a product under Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 shall be understood as including all AI systems falling within the scope of this Regulation.
@ref Art 74(1)(b) (src:1149)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system falls within the scope of this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(1)(b) the AI system is understood as a product under Regulation (EU) 2019/1020` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the AI system falls within the scope of this Regulation`
         THEN JUST TRUE  -- "shall be understood as including all AI systems falling within the scope of this Regulation"
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the text says what a reference is "understood as including"

§ `Article 74(2): reports of the market surveillance authorities`

-- src:1150 | 2. As part of their reporting obligations under Article 34(4) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, the market surveillance authorities shall report annually to the Commission and relevant national competition authorities any information identified in the course of market surveillance activities that may be of potential interest for the application of Union law on competition rules. They shall also annually report to the Commission about the use of prohibited practices that occurred during that year and about the measures taken.
@ref Art 74(2) first sentence (src:1150)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the market surveillance authorities have identified, in the course of market surveillance activities, information that may be of potential interest for the application of Union law on competition rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(2) first sentence the market surveillance authorities must report the information annually to the Commission and the relevant national competition authorities` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the market surveillance authorities have identified, in the course of market surveillance activities, information that may be of potential interest for the application of Union law on competition rules`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the report is of "any information identified ... that may be of potential interest for the application of Union law on competition rules"

-- src:1150 | 2. As part of their reporting obligations under Article 34(4) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, the market surveillance authorities shall report annually to the Commission and relevant national competition authorities any information identified in the course of market surveillance activities that may be of potential interest for the application of Union law on competition rules. They shall also annually report to the Commission about the use of prohibited practices that occurred during that year and about the measures taken.
@ref Art 74(2) second sentence (src:1150)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(2) second sentence the market surveillance authorities must report annually to the Commission about the use of prohibited practices and the measures taken` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE JUST TRUE  -- one answer: "They shall also annually report to the Commission about the use of prohibited practices that occurred during that year and about the measures taken"

-- src:1150 | 2. As part of their reporting obligations under Article 34(4) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, the market surveillance authorities shall report annually to the Commission and relevant national competition authorities any information identified in the course of market surveillance activities that may be of potential interest for the application of Union law on competition rules. They shall also annually report to the Commission about the use of prohibited practices that occurred during that year and about the measures taken.
@ref Art 74(2) first sentence (src:1150)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 74 act`
`Art 74(2) first sentence the market surveillance authorities' duty to report annually the information of interest for competition rules` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group General does not apply on the date asked
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party market surveillance authority`
        MUST `Art 74(2) report annually to the Commission and the relevant national competition authorities the information of potential interest for competition rules`
        HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:1150 | 2. As part of their reporting obligations under Article 34(4) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, the market surveillance authorities shall report annually to the Commission and relevant national competition authorities any information identified in the course of market surveillance activities that may be of potential interest for the application of Union law on competition rules. They shall also annually report to the Commission about the use of prohibited practices that occurred during that year and about the measures taken.
@ref Art 74(2) second sentence (src:1150)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 74 act`
`Art 74(2) second sentence the market surveillance authorities' duty to report annually about the use of prohibited practices` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group General does not apply on the date asked
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party market surveillance authority`
        MUST `Art 74(2) report annually to the Commission about the use of prohibited practices and the measures taken`
        HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Article 74(3): the market surveillance authority for a Section A system`

-- src:1151 | 3. For high-risk AI systems related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I, the market surveillance authority for the purposes of this Regulation shall be the authority responsible for market surveillance activities designated under those legal acts.
@ref Art 74(3) first subparagraph (src:1151)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system is a high-risk AI system related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(3) first subparagraph the market surveillance authority is the authority responsible for market surveillance activities designated under the Union harmonisation legislation` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the AI system is a high-risk AI system related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the first subparagraph is "For high-risk AI systems related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I" (a scope limit with no "only", ruling (c))

-- src:1152 | By derogation from the first subparagraph, and in appropriate circumstances, Member States may designate another relevant authority to act as a market surveillance authority, provided they ensure coordination with the relevant sectoral market surveillance authorities responsible for the enforcement of the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I.
@ref Art 74(3) second subparagraph (src:1152)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the circumstances are appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Member State ensures coordination with the relevant sectoral market surveillance authorities responsible for the enforcement of the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(3) second subparagraph the Member State may designate another relevant authority to act as a market surveillance authority` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF NOT `the circumstances are appropriate`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in appropriate circumstances" limits the power; the grant ruling of 2026-11-12 gives NOTHING for a failed "if"-type gate of a power (fork F-74-3-power)
         ELSE IF `the Member State ensures coordination with the relevant sectoral market surveillance authorities responsible for the enforcement of the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "provided they ensure coordination" limits the power (fork F-74-3-power)

§ `Article 74(4): the sectoral procedures replace Articles 79 to 83`

-- src:1153 | 4. The procedures referred to in Articles 79 to 83 of this Regulation shall not apply to AI systems related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in section A of Annex I, where such legal acts already provide for procedures ensuring an equivalent level of protection and having the same objective. In such cases, the relevant sectoral procedures shall apply instead.
@ref Art 74(4) (src:1153)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system is related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in section A of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those legal acts already provide for procedures ensuring an equivalent level of protection and having the same objective` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(4) the procedures referred to in Articles 79 to 83 do not apply to the AI system` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the AI system is related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in section A of Annex I` AND `those legal acts already provide for procedures ensuring an equivalent level of protection and having the same objective`
         THEN JUST TRUE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The procedures referred to in Articles 79 to 83 of this Regulation shall not apply" (a flat negative: they do not apply)
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the flat negative is limited to AI systems related to Section A products "where such legal acts already provide for procedures ensuring an equivalent level of protection and having the same objective"

-- src:1153 | 4. The procedures referred to in Articles 79 to 83 of this Regulation shall not apply to AI systems related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in section A of Annex I, where such legal acts already provide for procedures ensuring an equivalent level of protection and having the same objective. In such cases, the relevant sectoral procedures shall apply instead.
@ref Art 74(4) second sentence (src:1153)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system is related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in section A of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those legal acts already provide for procedures ensuring an equivalent level of protection and having the same objective` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(4) the relevant sectoral procedures apply instead` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the AI system is related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in section A of Annex I` AND `those legal acts already provide for procedures ensuring an equivalent level of protection and having the same objective`
         THEN JUST TRUE  -- "In such cases, the relevant sectoral procedures shall apply instead"
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In such cases" refers to the case of the first sentence

§ `Article 74(5): powers exercised remotely`

-- src:1154 | 5. Without prejudice to the powers of market surveillance authorities under Article 14 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, for the purpose of ensuring the effective enforcement of this Regulation, market surveillance authorities may exercise the powers referred to in Article 14(4), points (d) and (j), of that Regulation remotely, as appropriate.
@ref Art 74(5) (src:1154)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `it is appropriate to exercise the powers remotely` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(5) the market surveillance authority may exercise the powers referred to in Article 14(4), points (d) and (j), of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 remotely` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `it is appropriate to exercise the powers remotely`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as appropriate" limits the power; the grant ruling of 2026-11-12 gives NOTHING for a failed gate of a power (fork F-74-5-power)

§ `Article 74(6) and (7): the authority for a financial institution`

-- src:1155 | 6. For high-risk AI systems placed on the market, put into service, or used by financial institutions regulated by Union financial services law, the market surveillance authority for the purposes of this Regulation shall be the relevant national authority responsible for the financial supervision of those institutions under that legislation in so far as the placing on the market, putting into service, or the use of the AI system is in direct connection with the provision of those financial services.
@ref Art 74(6) (src:1155)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system is a high-risk AI system placed on the market, put into service, or used by a financial institution regulated by Union financial services law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the placing on the market, putting into service, or use of the AI system is in direct connection with the provision of those financial services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(6) the market surveillance authority is the relevant national authority responsible for the financial supervision of the institution` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the AI system is a high-risk AI system placed on the market, put into service, or used by a financial institution regulated by Union financial services law` AND `the placing on the market, putting into service, or use of the AI system is in direct connection with the provision of those financial services`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 6 is for high-risk AI systems of financial institutions "in so far as" the use is in direct connection with the provision of financial services

-- src:1156 | 7. By way of derogation from paragraph 6, in appropriate circumstances, and provided that coordination is ensured, another relevant authority may be identified by the Member State as market surveillance authority for the purposes of this Regulation.
@ref Art 74(7) first subparagraph (src:1156)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the circumstances are appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `coordination is ensured` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(7) first subparagraph the Member State may identify another relevant authority as market surveillance authority` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF NOT `the circumstances are appropriate`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in appropriate circumstances" limits the power (fork F-74-3-power)
         ELSE IF `coordination is ensured`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "provided that coordination is ensured" limits the power (fork F-74-3-power)

-- src:1157 | National market surveillance authorities supervising regulated credit institutions regulated under Directive 2013/36/EU, which are participating in the Single Supervisory Mechanism established by Regulation (EU) No 1024/2013, should report, without delay, to the European Central Bank any information identified in the course of their market surveillance activities that may be of potential interest for the prudential supervisory tasks of the European Central Bank specified in that Regulation.
@ref Art 74(7) second subparagraph (src:1157)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the market surveillance authority supervises regulated credit institutions regulated under Directive 2013/36/EU` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those credit institutions participate in the Single Supervisory Mechanism established by Regulation (EU) No 1024/2013` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authority has identified in the course of its market surveillance activities information that may be of potential interest for the prudential supervisory tasks of the European Central Bank` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(7) second subparagraph the market surveillance authority should report the information without delay to the European Central Bank` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the market surveillance authority supervises regulated credit institutions regulated under Directive 2013/36/EU` AND `those credit institutions participate in the Single Supervisory Mechanism established by Regulation (EU) No 1024/2013` AND `the authority has identified in the course of its market surveillance activities information that may be of potential interest for the prudential supervisory tasks of the European Central Bank`
         THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says "should report", not "shall report" (fork F-74-7-should)
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about authorities supervising regulated credit institutions in the Single Supervisory Mechanism and information of potential interest for the ECB's prudential tasks

§ `Article 74(8) and (9): designations`

-- src:1158 | 8. For high-risk AI systems listed in point 1 of Annex III to this Regulation, in so far as the systems are used for law enforcement purposes, border management and justice and democracy, and for high-risk AI systems listed in points 6, 7 and 8 of Annex III to this Regulation, Member States shall designate as market surveillance authorities for the purposes of this Regulation either the competent data protection supervisory authorities under Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or Directive (EU) 2016/680, or any other authority designated pursuant to the same conditions laid down in Articles 41 to 44 of Directive (EU) 2016/680. Market surveillance activities shall in no way affect the independence of judicial authorities, or otherwise interfere with their activities when acting in their judicial capacity.
@ref Art 74(8) first sentence (src:1158)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system is listed in point 1 of Annex III and is used for law enforcement purposes, border management or justice and democracy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the AI system is listed in point 6, 7 or 8 of Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(8) first sentence the Member State must designate as market surveillance authority a data protection supervisory authority or another authority designated under Directive (EU) 2016/680` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the AI system is listed in point 1 of Annex III and is used for law enforcement purposes, border management or justice and democracy` OR `the AI system is listed in point 6, 7 or 8 of Annex III`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the designation is for the high-risk AI systems "listed in point 1 of Annex III ... in so far as ... used for law enforcement purposes, border management and justice and democracy, and for ... points 6, 7 and 8 of Annex III"

-- src:1158 | 8. For high-risk AI systems listed in point 1 of Annex III to this Regulation, in so far as the systems are used for law enforcement purposes, border management and justice and democracy, and for high-risk AI systems listed in points 6, 7 and 8 of Annex III to this Regulation, Member States shall designate as market surveillance authorities for the purposes of this Regulation either the competent data protection supervisory authorities under Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or Directive (EU) 2016/680, or any other authority designated pursuant to the same conditions laid down in Articles 41 to 44 of Directive (EU) 2016/680. Market surveillance activities shall in no way affect the independence of judicial authorities, or otherwise interfere with their activities when acting in their judicial capacity.
@ref Art 74(8) second sentence (src:1158)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the authority is a judicial authority acting in its judicial capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(8) second sentence the market surveillance activities are barred from affecting the independence of the judicial authority or interfering with its activities` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the authority is a judicial authority acting in its judicial capacity`
         THEN JUST TRUE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Market surveillance activities shall in no way affect the independence of judicial authorities, or otherwise interfere with their activities when acting in their judicial capacity" (a flat negative: the bar holds)
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is for judicial authorities, and the interference limb "when acting in their judicial capacity"

-- src:1158 | 8. For high-risk AI systems listed in point 1 of Annex III to this Regulation, in so far as the systems are used for law enforcement purposes, border management and justice and democracy, and for high-risk AI systems listed in points 6, 7 and 8 of Annex III to this Regulation, Member States shall designate as market surveillance authorities for the purposes of this Regulation either the competent data protection supervisory authorities under Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or Directive (EU) 2016/680, or any other authority designated pursuant to the same conditions laid down in Articles 41 to 44 of Directive (EU) 2016/680. Market surveillance activities shall in no way affect the independence of judicial authorities, or otherwise interfere with their activities when acting in their judicial capacity.
@ref Art 74(8) first sentence (src:1158)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 74 act`
`Art 74(8) first sentence the Member State's duty to designate the market surveillance authorities` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group General does not apply on the date asked
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party Member State`
        MUST `Art 74(8) designate as market surveillance authorities the data protection supervisory authorities or another authority`
        HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:1159 | 9. Where Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies fall within the scope of this Regulation, the European Data Protection Supervisor shall act as their market surveillance authority, except in relation to the Court of Justice of the European Union acting in its judicial capacity.
@ref Art 74(9) (src:1159)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies fall within the scope of this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Union body is the Court of Justice of the European Union acting in its judicial capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(9) the European Data Protection Supervisor acts as the market surveillance authority` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF NOT `Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies fall within the scope of this Regulation`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies fall within the scope of this Regulation"
         ELSE IF `the Union body is the Court of Justice of the European Union acting in its judicial capacity`
              THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except in relation to the Court of Justice of the European Union acting in its judicial capacity"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Article 74(10) and (11): coordination and joint activities`

-- src:1160 | 10. Member States shall facilitate coordination between market surveillance authorities designated under this Regulation and other relevant national authorities or bodies which supervise the application of Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I, or in other Union law, that might be relevant for the high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III.
@ref Art 74(10) (src:1160)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(10) the Member States must facilitate coordination between the market surveillance authorities and other relevant national authorities or bodies` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE JUST TRUE  -- one answer: "Member States shall facilitate coordination"

-- src:1160 | 10. Member States shall facilitate coordination between market surveillance authorities designated under this Regulation and other relevant national authorities or bodies which supervise the application of Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I, or in other Union law, that might be relevant for the high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III.
@ref Art 74(10) (src:1160)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 74 act`
`Art 74(10) the Member States' duty to facilitate coordination` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group General does not apply on the date asked
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party Member State`
        MUST `Art 74(10) facilitate coordination between market surveillance authorities and other relevant national authorities or bodies`
        HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:1161 | 11. Market surveillance authorities and the Commission shall be able to propose joint activities, including joint investigations, to be conducted by either market surveillance authorities or market surveillance authorities jointly with the Commission, that have the aim of promoting compliance, identifying non-compliance, raising awareness or providing guidance in relation to this Regulation with respect to specific categories of high-risk AI systems that are found to present a serious risk across two or more Member States in accordance with Article 9 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020. The AI Office shall provide coordination support for joint investigations.
@ref Art 74(11) first sentence (src:1161)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the activities are proposed with respect to specific categories of high-risk AI systems that are found to present a serious risk across two or more Member States in accordance with Article 9 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activities have the aim of promoting compliance, identifying non-compliance, raising awareness or providing guidance in relation to this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(11) first sentence the market surveillance authorities and the Commission are able to propose joint activities, including joint investigations` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the activities are proposed with respect to specific categories of high-risk AI systems that are found to present a serious risk across two or more Member States in accordance with Article 9 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020` AND `the activities have the aim of promoting compliance, identifying non-compliance, raising awareness or providing guidance in relation to this Regulation`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is for activities "that have the aim of" these purposes "with respect to specific categories of high-risk AI systems that are found to present a serious risk across two or more Member States"

-- src:1161 | 11. Market surveillance authorities and the Commission shall be able to propose joint activities, including joint investigations, to be conducted by either market surveillance authorities or market surveillance authorities jointly with the Commission, that have the aim of promoting compliance, identifying non-compliance, raising awareness or providing guidance in relation to this Regulation with respect to specific categories of high-risk AI systems that are found to present a serious risk across two or more Member States in accordance with Article 9 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020. The AI Office shall provide coordination support for joint investigations.
@ref Art 74(11) second sentence (src:1161)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `a joint investigation is conducted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(11) second sentence the AI Office must provide coordination support for the joint investigation` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `a joint investigation is conducted`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall provide coordination support for joint investigations" gives no duty where there is no joint investigation (an unmet gate of a duty counts as the text's no: marginal reading (a)) (fork F-74-11-second-duty)

-- src:1161 | 11. Market surveillance authorities and the Commission shall be able to propose joint activities, including joint investigations, to be conducted by either market surveillance authorities or market surveillance authorities jointly with the Commission, that have the aim of promoting compliance, identifying non-compliance, raising awareness or providing guidance in relation to this Regulation with respect to specific categories of high-risk AI systems that are found to present a serious risk across two or more Member States in accordance with Article 9 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020. The AI Office shall provide coordination support for joint investigations.
@ref Art 74(11) second sentence (src:1161)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `a joint investigation is conducted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 74 act`
`Art 74(11) second sentence the AI Office's duty to provide coordination support` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)) OR (NOT `a joint investigation is conducted`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group General does not apply on the date asked, or there is no joint investigation
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party AI Office`
        MUST `Art 74(11) provide coordination support for joint investigations`
        HENCE FULFILLED

§ `Article 74(12) and (13): what the provider must give the market surveillance authority`

-- "Without prejudice to the powers provided for under Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, and where relevant and limited to what is necessary to fulfil their tasks, the market
-- surveillance authorities shall be granted full access by providers to the documentation as well as the training, validation and testing data sets ..."
-- src:1162 | 12. Without prejudice to the powers provided for under Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, and where relevant and limited to what is necessary to fulfil their tasks, the market surveillance authorities shall be granted full access by providers to the documentation as well as the training, validation and testing data sets used for the development of high-risk AI systems, including, where appropriate and subject to security safeguards, through application programming interfaces (API) or other relevant technical means and tools enabling remote access.
@ref Art 74(12) (src:1162)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `full access is relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `full access is limited to what is necessary to fulfil the market surveillance authority's tasks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(12) the provider must grant the market surveillance authority full access to the documentation and the training, validation and testing data sets` MEANS
    IF `Arts 72 to 79 Article 2(2) cuts off the provision` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 74 12
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives, and Art 111(2) saves a high-risk AI system placed earlier and not significantly changed
         ELSE IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the AI system is a high-risk AI system` `the route to high-risk`)
              THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the provision speaks of high-risk AI systems
              ELSE IF `full access is relevant` AND `full access is limited to what is necessary to fulfil the market surveillance authority's tasks`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where relevant and limited to what is necessary to fulfil their tasks" (an unmet "where" gate counts as the text's no: ruling (b) of 2026-11-05) (fork F-74-12-duty)

-- src:1162 | 12. Without prejudice to the powers provided for under Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, and where relevant and limited to what is necessary to fulfil their tasks, the market surveillance authorities shall be granted full access by providers to the documentation as well as the training, validation and testing data sets used for the development of high-risk AI systems, including, where appropriate and subject to security safeguards, through application programming interfaces (API) or other relevant technical means and tools enabling remote access.
@ref Art 74(12) (src:1162)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `full access is relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `full access is limited to what is necessary to fulfil the market surveillance authority's tasks` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has granted full access to the documentation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has granted full access to the training, validation and testing data sets` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(12) the provider has granted the market surveillance authority full access to the documentation and the data sets` MEANS
    IF `Arts 72 to 79 Article 2(2) cuts off the provision` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 74 12
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE CONSIDER `Art 74(12) the provider must grant the market surveillance authority full access to the documentation and the training, validation and testing data sets` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `full access is relevant` `full access is limited to what is necessary to fulfil the market surveillance authority's tasks`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST (`the provider has granted full access to the documentation` AND `the provider has granted full access to the training, validation and testing data sets`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be granted full access by providers to the documentation as well as the training, validation and testing data sets" (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)
         OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): no duty to grant full access arises on these facts (see the function above)

