§ `Article 74(14): confidentiality`

-- src:1166 | 14. Any information or documentation obtained by market surveillance authorities shall be treated in accordance with the confidentiality obligations set out in Article 78.
@ref Art 74(14) (src:1166)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the information or documentation has been obtained by the market surveillance authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(14) the information or documentation obtained by the market surveillance authority is to be treated in accordance with Article 78` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group General applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the information or documentation has been obtained by the market surveillance authority`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "Any information or documentation obtained by market surveillance authorities"

